  "source_review": [
    "All native optional GUI paths test main-thread status before reading editor fields; worker hint performs caller-locked numerical work without GUI pointer reads. Dispatcher attach/detach, Idle and destruction likewise guard before accesses.",
    "Editor creation rejects unmatched lock pairs. Refresh snapshots all5 raw values under a paired host lock, then updates AppKit controls after unlock. Change sets numerical value under lock; changed/hint callbacks and follow-up refresh occur after unlock.",
    "Main native hint calls internally lock their numerical get/set work, notify after unlock. Contract explicitly requires those main hint calls outside the caller nonrecursive mix lock. Worker numerical/state/render calls remain caller serialized.",
    "Tick and MIDI tick are effect no-ops. Optional native off-main destruction, even before first attachment, leaves the numerical/native/view objects alive. Host wrapper, context and module must remain valid through main retry. Destruction/render lifetime excludes concurrent unsynchronized teardown.",
    "Restore reads a single20-byte packet into local storage via uint32 transfer length, signed32 HRESULT and zeroed wide completion storage. C API validates all5 raw fields before committing state; host quality remains selected externally.",
    "Default no-editor compiled candidate exercises all20 callbacks and actual intact-engine DLL loader. Real TMemoryStream/TStreamAdapter checks actual signed32 HRESULT and32-bit completion stores with adjacent sentinels.",
    "Extra20 malformed optional-editor packets at min-1/max+1/INT_MIN/INT_MAX across all5 fields preserve raw bytes, coefficient bits and interpolated output. Numeric FP/alias/range contracts stay those of separately accepted bounded API."
  ],
  "caller_contracts": {
    "numerical": "fast_dist_plugin.h preserved5raw/ranges,coef/state/default integer quality0 contracts.",
    "main_thread": "Every GUI operation/read/destruction guarded before touching GUI-owned fields. Worker tick/MIDI/Idle/hint do not access GUI. Off-main native destruction even beforeattachment refuses, preserving native object/numerical state; caller retains original wrapper/host/context/modules until main retry.",
    "mix_lock": "GUI snapshots/control changes under valid paired host32/33; notifications/resize/hints after unlock. Main hint4 calls outside caller lock; internal paired lock serializes numerical getter/set work. Worker numerical/native calls stay caller-serialized.",
    "quality": "Standalone own quality0/1 discriminating probes, optional preset32saves/restores preserve selected mode; quality production remains caller controlled. Concurrent renderer uses explicit integer0, snapshots20bytes to worker-owned reference, compares every8frame block and sees nonidentity audio."
  },
